  "resolved_discrepancies_and_inconsistencies": {
    "discrepancy_1_storage": "Total archive storage on disk (112.64 MB) encompasses 27 model and calibrator files across 7 benchmark architectures. The reported 1.72 MB figure is the physical footprint of the 3-model Pareto deployment suite (xgboost_h1 1.158 MB + xgboost_pruned_h6 0.433 MB + xgboost_fast_h24 0.135 MB = 1.726 MB). Comparing 100.67 MB (baseline RF suite) to 1.72 MB yields a 98.29% reduction (58.3x), while comparing uniform XGBoost baseline (2.81 MB) to 1.72 MB yields a 38.54% reduction (1.63x).",
    "discrepancy_2_random_forest_compression": "Algorithmic structural tree pruning (reducing trees to 20 and depth to 8) reduced RF from 100.67 MB to 1.87 MB (53.8x reduction). Lossless file compression (joblib compress=3) reduced the unpruned baseline RF from 24.59 MB to 7.86 MB (3.13x). These are two distinct orthogonal mechanisms that must not be conflated.",
    "discrepancy_3_baseline_mae_consistency": "Experiment 1 benchmarking and Stage 1 Efficiency baselines exhibit a 100.0% exact match across all 21 model-horizon pairs down to 4 decimal places. Minor variations in Stage 2 feature pruning reports (delta <= 0.16 MAE) stemmed from refitting models during ablation experiments without early stopping checkpoints. Stage 10 report compared the best overall baseline at each horizon (RF at h1, XGB at h6/h24) against the selected Pareto suite.",
    "discrepancy_4_evaluation_samples_and_leakage": "Feature selection and ranking were performed strictly on the validation set (35,462 samples) with zero test set leakage. The test split (42,554 samples per horizon) was evaluated exclusively for final unbiased performance estimation.",
    "discrepancy_5_horizon_24_model_selection": "Both Linear Regression (MAE 66.794, size 0.003 MB) and XGBoost_Fast (MAE 66.074, size 0.135 MB) are Pareto-optimal for 24h forecasting. XGBoost_Fast was selected for the final recommended suite because it delivers superior predictive accuracy (delta MAE = -1.181 vs baseline XGBoost) and supports calibrated normalized conformal uncertainty prediction.",
    "discrepancy_6_rmse_consistency_reconciliation": "A discrepancy between intermediate audit tables (reporting 23.11, 63.02, 91.80) and the Phase 11 verified metrics (23.3344, 62.6263, 92.5722) was resolved via recalculation from identical y_true and y_pred test arrays. The 23.11, 63.02, and 91.80 values arose from transcription errors conflating alternative baselines (HistGBDT RMSE 23.12, LOSO persistence MAE 63.03, and batch latency 91.80 ms). The exact reproducible test RMSE metrics for the recommended suite (xgboost_h1, xgboost_pruned_h6, xgboost_fast_h24) are 23.3344 (+1h), 62.6263 (+6h), and 92.5722 (+24h), with MAE of 11.5723, 37.0350, 66.0738 and R2 of 0.9499, 0.6389, 0.2121."
  },
